H('416.d.12.F',3,"Level of service is graded from A to F, where A represents the:","best operating conditions",["worst conditions","most expensive road","longest road"],"LOS A is free flow.")
H('416.d.12.F',4,"A roadway that operates at level of service F is experiencing:","severe congestion",["free-flowing traffic","empty lanes","no vehicles"],"LOS F means breakdown.")
H('416.d.12.G',3,"A traffic impact analysis estimates how much new traffic a development will add and its effect on nearby:","intersections",["pet stores","parks only","vacations"],"TIAs study local impacts.")
H('416.d.12.G',4,"Typical TIA components include trip generation, trip distribution, and an evaluation of the roadway's:","capacity",["wallpaper","mascot","brand voice"],"TIAs compare demand to capacity.")
H('416.d.12.H',3,"Traffic data can be collected with tube counters, video cameras, or manual:","counts",["lyrics","menus","recipes"],"Several methods exist.")
H('416.d.12.H',4,"Pneumatic road tubes count vehicles by sensing the pulses of air created when tires:","cross them",["pass overhead","warm up","rust"],"Tubes detect axle hits.")
H('416.d.12.I',3,"A manual count records 120 vehicles in one hour. The hourly volume is:","120 vehicles per hour",["12 vehicles per hour","1,200 vehicles per hour","60 vehicles per hour"],"The count already covers one hour.")
H('416.d.12.I',4,"If a count shows 300 vehicles in 15 minutes, the equivalent hourly flow rate is:","1,200 vehicles per hour",["300 vehicles per hour","900 vehicles per hour","4,500 vehicles per hour"],"300 x 4 = 1,200.")
H('416.d.12.J',3,"The ITE Trip Generation Manual gives the number of trips a land use produces per unit such as per 1,000 square feet or per:","dwelling unit",["tree","sign","school bell"],"Trip rates depend on land use.")
H('416.d.12.J',4,"A store of 20 thousand square feet has a rate of 3 peak-hour trips per 1,000 square feet. Its peak-hour trips are:","60",["23","6","600"],"20 x 3 = 60.")
H('416.d.12.K',3,"Level of service for a road is based on measures like delay and speed relative to the road's:","capacity",["color","age","slogan"],"LOS compares demand to capacity.")
H('416.d.12.K',4,"At a signalized intersection, level of service is often found from the average delay each vehicle experiences, measured in:","seconds",["acres","pounds","degrees"],"Delay is measured in seconds per vehicle.")
H('416.d.12.L',3,"A turn lane is warranted when the number of turning vehicles is high enough to cause delay or safety problems for the:","through traffic",["parking","pedestrian art","utility lines"],"Turn lanes remove turners from the through lane.")
H('416.d.12.L',4,"If the left-turn volume exceeds the guideline for a given opposing volume, the engineer should recommend a:","left-turn lane",["stop to a dead end","lower speed limit only","wider sidewalk only"],"Warrants justify added lanes.")
H('416.d.12.M',3,"A transportation analysis showing long delays could lead to changes in the site's driveway locations or the:","number of access points",["owner's name","paint color","lobby music"],"Analysis may change access.")
H('416.d.12.M',4,"A positive result from a transportation analysis helps the project win approval from the:","city or state agency",["competing firm","weather service","social club"],"Agencies review traffic studies.")
H('416.d.13.A',3,"Construction documents include design plans, specifications, and the:","bid forms and contract terms",["lunch menu","staff photos","music list"],"Documents define what is built.")
H('416.d.13.A',4,"Construction documents must be complete and clear so the contractor can build and the owner can:","verify compliance",["avoid payment","change the project at will","skip inspections"],"Documents govern construction.")
H('416.d.13.B',3,"Analysis reports for a civil project, such as drainage, geotechnical, and traffic reports, support the design:","decisions",["jokes","hobbies","moods"],"Reports justify decisions.")
H('416.d.13.B',4,"Analysis reports are submitted to reviewing agencies so they can confirm the design meets the:","regulations",["owner's taste","firm's logo","engineer's hobbies"],"Agencies verify compliance.")
H('416.d.13.C',3,"A demolition sheet shows what existing features will be:","removed",["added","painted","renamed"],"Demolition sheets show removals.")
H('416.d.13.C',4,"Existing topography, property lines, and utilities appear on a demolition sheet so the contractor knows what must be protected or:","taken out",["advertised","saved as art","copied"],"Existing conditions guide removals.")
H('416.d.13.D',3,"A fire protection plan shows hydrant locations, fire lanes, and building:","access for fire trucks",["interior color","tenant names","bike racks only"],"Fire access is essential.")
H('416.d.13.D',4,"A fire lane must be wide enough and have a turning radius large enough for a:","fire apparatus",["bicycle","wheelbarrow","sled"],"Fire trucks need room.")
H('416.d.13.E',3,"A paving plan shows the limits of the pavement and the type of surface, such as asphalt or:","concrete",["velvet","paper","wood chips"],"Pavement types are shown.")
H('416.d.13.E',4,"A paving plan also gives pavement section details and the locations of joints and:","curbs",["art","dances","menus"],"Details guide construction.")
H('416.d.13.F',3,"A site plan that labels proposed improvements shows the locations of buildings, driveways, and:","parking areas",["lunch trucks","family photos","business cards"],"Site plans show layout.")
H('416.d.13.F',4,"A site plan must show setbacks so that reviewers can confirm the proposed buildings are placed where the code:","allows",["forbids","ignores","hides"],"Setbacks limit placement.")
H('416.d.13.G',3,"A site dimensional control plan gives measurements so the contractor can lay out buildings and curbs in the correct:","locations",["colors","moods","names"],"Control plans guide layout.")
H('416.d.13.G',4,"A dimension control plan ties building corners to fixed reference points such as property corners or survey:","benchmarks",["billboards","cartoons","menus"],"Reference points anchor layout.")
H('416.d.13.H',3,"A grading plan shows existing and proposed ground heights using contours and spot:","elevations",["colors","logos","names"],"Grading plans show heights.")
H('416.d.13.H',4,"A grading plan is designed so surface water flows away from buildings and toward drains at a minimum:","slope",["color","price","width"],"Positive drainage prevents ponding.")
H('416.d.13.I',3,"A drainage plan shows existing and proposed flow patterns, inlets, and pipes so water is directed to the:","outlet",["lobby","playground only","roof"],"Drainage plans route runoff.")
H('416.d.13.I',4,"A drainage plan may show a swale or inlet at low points to prevent water from standing on the:","pavement",["ceiling","wall paint","equipment catalog"],"Low points need inlets.")
H('416.d.13.J',3,"A utility plan shows the locations of water lines, sewer lines, and electric and gas lines that serve the:","site",["weather","bank","calendar"],"Utility plans show services.")
H('416.d.13.J',4,"On a utility plan, proposed and existing utilities are shown with different line styles so the contractor can tell what is:","new versus old",["pretty versus ugly","loud versus quiet","hot versus cold"],"Line styles communicate status.")
H('416.d.13.K',3,"An erosion control plan identifies best management practices, such as silt fences and construction:","entrances",["trophies","parties","logos"],"BMPs keep sediment on site.")
H('416.d.13.K',4,"A stabilized construction entrance reduces the amount of mud that trucks carry onto:","public roads",["private offices","parking meters","school buses only"],"Entrances shed mud.")
H('416.d.13.L',3,"A quality control review finds errors and conflicts in the plans before they are issued for:","construction",["a vacation","a party","a game"],"QC prevents costly mistakes.")
H('416.d.13.L',4,"A QC reviewer who is not the original designer is more likely to catch mistakes because of a fresh:","perspective",["lunch","password","paycheck"],"Independent review finds more errors.")
H('416.d.14.A',3,"A bid tabulation lists each item's description, quantity, unit, unit price, and:","extended price",["color","owner","slogan"],"Extension = quantity x unit price.")
H('416.d.14.A',4,"A bid item of 500 linear feet of pipe at 30 dollars per foot has an extended price of:","15,000 dollars",["530 dollars","1,500 dollars","150 dollars"],"500 x 30 = 15,000.")
H('416.d.14.B',3,"Comparing a bid tabulation with the construction documents ensures every item in the plans appears in the:","bid",["menu","poster","playlist"],"Missing items cause cost surprises.")
H('416.d.14.B',4,"If a bidder leaves out a pay item that appears in the plans, the engineer should flag the bid as:","incomplete",["perfect","finalized","lowest by default"],"Complete bids include every item.")
H('416.d.14.C',3,"To create a bid tabulation for a project, the engineer lists all pay items and the bids from each:","contractor",["tourist","competitor's cousin","journalist"],"Tabs organize bid results.")
H('416.d.14.C',4,"The total bid is found by adding the extended prices of all the:","bid items",["bidders","pages","signatures"],"Totals sum the items.")
H('416.d.14.D',3,"The project manual contains the bidding requirements, contract forms, and the:","technical specifications",["lunch order","vacation photos","staff gossip"],"The manual bundles documents.")
H('416.d.14.D',4,"Organizing a project manual in the standard order helps bidders find the information they need to prepare an accurate:","price",["dinner","playlist","alarm"],"Organization helps bidders.")
H('416.d.15.A',3,"A manager who compares completed tasks with the schedule is tracking whether team goals and project:","milestones are being met",["colors are matching","logos are on time","cars are parked"],"Tracking shows progress.")
H('416.d.15.A',4,"If a milestone is missed, the manager should find the cause and adjust the:","plan",["milestone's name","office carpet","uniforms"],"Tracking supports correction.")
H('416.d.15.B',3,"One effective method for resolving conflict on a project team is to listen to each person and focus on the:","problem, not the person",["person, not the problem","loudest voice","oldest member"],"Constructive conflict focuses on issues.")
H('416.d.15.B',4,"When two engineers disagree about a design choice, a good first step is to compare each option to the:","project requirements",["office mood","weather forecast","time of day"],"Requirements provide an objective basis.")
H('416.d.15.C',3,"Leaders who communicate clear goals and recognize good work help team members stay:","motivated",["confused","isolated","bored"],"Leadership shapes morale.")
H('416.d.15.C',4,"A project leader who ignores team input risks lower team member:","engagement",["salary","height","age"],"People disengage when unheard.")
H('416.d.15.D',3,"Evaluating a teammate's performance should be based on specific, observable:","contributions",["rumors","guesses","appearances"],"Evidence-based feedback is fair.")
H('416.d.15.D',4,"Effective performance feedback names what was done well and what could be done to:","improve",["hide","punish","delay"],"Balanced feedback helps growth.")
H('416.d.16.A',3,"The Texas Engineering Practice Act regulates who may offer engineering services and requires a:","license",["mascot","uniform","logo"],"The Act protects the public.")
H('416.d.16.A',4,"Offering engineering services to the public in Texas without being licensed can result in:","penalties",["rewards","promotions","tax credits"],"Unlicensed practice is illegal.")
H('416.d.16.B',3,"Texas Administrative Code Chapter 137 includes rules of conduct for engineers that require them to hold paramount the public's:","safety, health, and welfare",["entertainment","comfort","opinion"],"Rules put safety first.")
H('416.d.16.B',4,"An ethical case study may describe an engineer who was pressured to approve a faulty design. The best response under the code is to:","refuse and report",["approve quietly","delete the report","blame a coworker"],"Duty to the public overrides pressure.")
H('416.d.17.A',3,"Using recycled steel, reclaimed wood, or low-carbon concrete are examples of sustainable building:","materials",["fashions","songs","captions"],"Sustainable materials reduce impact.")
H('416.d.17.A',4,"Designing a building to use daylight and well-insulated walls is a sustainable method that reduces:","energy use",["tenant count","window area to zero","site size"],"Efficient design cuts energy.")
H('416.d.17.B',3,"LEED is a program that certifies buildings designed to meet defined standards for:","sustainability",["decoration","size","location only"],"LEED rates green performance.")
H('416.d.17.B',4,"Envision is a rating system used for sustainable civil projects such as roads, pipelines, and:","water systems",["office lobbies","clothing stores","sports bars"],"Envision covers infrastructure.")
H('416.d.17.C',3,"A project that earns a sustainability certification may qualify for incentives and attract tenants who value:","green buildings",["noise","waste","delays"],"Certification can add value.")
H('416.d.17.C',4,"Pursuing certification typically adds documentation requirements and design effort, which can affect the project's:","cost and schedule",["mascot","slogan","address"],"Certification has trade-offs.")
H('416.d.17.D',3,"Design choices such as adding trees and permeable pavement can improve air quality and reduce:","stormwater runoff",["property lines","traffic signs","building codes"],"Green features help the environment.")
H('416.d.17.D',4,"Indoor air quality, lighting, and acoustics are design factors that affect human:","health and comfort",["tax rates","street names","office hours"],"Design shapes well-being.")
H('416.d.17.E',3,"Construction dust, noise, and runoff can affect the health of workers and nearby:","residents",["calendars","coupons","statues"],"Construction has impacts.")
H('416.d.17.E',4,"A contractor who covers stockpiles and wets disturbed soil is limiting airborne:","dust",["music","paint","light"],"Dust control protects health.")
H('417. d.1',3,"A consulting engineer learns that a client's building plan skips a required fire exit to save money. Ethics requires her to:","insist on the code-required exit",["quietly omit the exit","stamp it as is","let the client decide alone"],"Public safety outranks client cost wishes.")
H('417. d.1',4,"An engineer discovers an error in a bridge calculation she already sealed. The ethical action is to:","notify the client and correct it",["say nothing","blame the software","wait for an inspection"],"Honesty about errors protects the public.")
H('417. d.2.A',3,"A transit agency wants shorter bus waits. Writing down exactly what delays buses is the design process step of:","defining the problem",["buying the buses","picking a paint color","choosing a mascot"],"A well-defined problem comes first.")
H('417. d.2.A',4,"Defining an engineering problem carefully matters because a solution to the wrong question will:","waste time and money",["win awards","save money","need no testing"],"Wrong problem, wrong solution.")
H('417. d.2.B',3,"In the research stage, a team designing a bike path gathers crash records, user counts, and existing:","design guidelines",["song lyrics","menu prices","jersey colors"],"Research collects relevant data.")
H('417. d.2.B',4,"Reviewing how other cities built protected bike lanes helps a team learn what has and has not:","worked in practice",["been advertised","been named","been funded by tourists"],"Precedents guide design.")
H('417. d.2.C',3,"Brainstorming ten ways to cool a plaza, such as shade sails, trees, and misters, is called:","ideation",["inspection","depreciation","closeout"],"Ideation generates options.")
H('417. d.2.C',4,"Turning the shade-sail idea into a sketch with dimensions and materials moves the team from ideation to:","conceptualization",["abandonment","litigation","retirement"],"Concepts develop ideas into rough designs.")
H('417. d.2.D',3,"A team ranks four stormwater options against cost, maintenance, and space needed. This process is:","selecting a concept",["naming a pond","closing a contract","filing a permit"],"Selection uses criteria.")
H('417. d.2.D',4,"A decision matrix gives each option a weighted score so the choice rests on the criteria rather than on:","personal preference alone",["measured data","project goals","client needs"],"Matrices add objectivity.")
H('417. d.2.E',3,"A freehand doodle on a napkin is informal, while a scaled plan sheet with dimensions is a:","technical drawing",["cartoon","greeting card","poster"],"Technical drawings follow standards.")
H('417. d.2.E',4,"A small physical model of a building is built mainly to help clients and teams:","visualize the design",["avoid permits","hide the cost","skip inspection"],"Models communicate form.")
H('417. d.2.F',3,"Before pouring a full-size slab, a lab tests small concrete samples to learn how the mix will:","perform under load",["look at night","cost less","sound when struck"],"Tests predict real behavior.")
H('417. d.2.F',4,"A well-designed experiment changes one factor at a time, such as water content, so the effect of that factor is:","clear to the tester",["hidden","random","meaningless"],"Controlled tests isolate causes.")
H('417. d.2.G',3,"When a trial pond layout drains too slowly, the team adjusts the outlet size and checks again, showing the process is:","repeated as needed",["done once","random","unscientific"],"Iteration refines the design.")
H('417. d.2.G',4,"Feedback from reviewers and test data plays a role in iteration by showing the team what to:","change next",["ignore","hide","delete"],"Feedback drives the next version.")
H('417. d.2.H',3,"Sharing a finished design with the public through clear drawings and plain explanations is effective:","communication",["isolation","secrecy","delay"],"Communication transfers the solution.")
H('417. d.2.H',4,"Communicating the engineering solution to a contractor with clear drawings reduces the chance of:","misinterpretation",["profits","inspections","approvals"],"Clear documents prevent errors.")
H('417. d.3.A',3,"A junior engineer lists the week's tasks in order of due date and importance. This is a time-management strategy called:","prioritizing",["avoiding","guessing","delaying"],"Prioritization manages time.")
H('417. d.3.A',4,"Setting a deadline two days before the real due date leaves room to handle:","unexpected problems",["lunch","paint","music"],"Buffers absorb surprises.")
H('417. d.3.B',3,"A project that cannot be built in the rainy season because crews cannot place concrete in the wet faces a:","weather constraint",["fashion constraint","music constraint","paint constraint"],"Constraints come from conditions.")
H('417. d.3.B',4,"Planning around a constraint such as a utility shutdown window means scheduling the affected work during the:","allowed period",["off hours of nothing","wrong season","last day of the contract"],"Plans fit constraints.")
H('417. d.3.C',3,"Delivering the soil report on June 1 and the grading plan on July 1 are examples of project:","deliverables and milestones",["rumors","vacations","hobbies"],"Deliverables mark progress.")
H('417. d.3.C',4,"Dividing a long project into smaller deliverables helps a manager catch trouble:","sooner",["later","never","after closing"],"Short checkpoints reveal problems.")
H('417. d.3.D',3,"A text message to a coworker asking for a file is informal, while a sealed letter to a client is:","formal communication",["a rumor","small talk","a joke"],"Formality varies with purpose.")
H('417. d.3.D',4,"Choosing a phone call over email for an urgent site issue works because it provides:","immediate feedback",["a permanent record only","a lower cost only","less clarity"],"Mode affects speed.")
H('417. d.3.E',3,"When a pipe will not fit, a team lists possible causes and tests them one at a time, using the strategy of:","systematic troubleshooting",["wishful thinking","random guessing","giving up"],"Systematic methods solve problems.")
H('417. d.3.E',4,"Problem solving works better when a team shares what each member knows because it widens the set of:","possible solutions",["problems","excuses","delays"],"Collaboration adds ideas.")
H('417. d.4.A',3,"Under federal law, a contractor must give crews training, protective gear, and a worksite with no known serious:","hazards",["breaks","paychecks","schedules"],"Employers must provide safe work.")
H('417. d.4.A',4,"A worker who sees a damaged scaffold plank has a responsibility to avoid using it and to:","report it",["paint it","hide it","remove the sign"],"Workers share safety duties.")
H('417. d.4.B',3,"A federal agency that sets and enforces workplace safety rules, including those for trenching, is:","OSHA",["NASA","NOAA","FEMA"],"OSHA regulates workplace safety.")
H('417. d.4.B',4,"OSHA requires a trench deeper than five feet to have a protective system because cave-ins can cause:","fatal injuries",["extra shade","faster work","lower pay"],"Trenching is a leading cause of death.")
H('417. d.4.C',3,"An industrial hygienist measuring silica dust at a saw-cutting site is trying to prevent long-term:","lung disease",["bad grammar","low pay","slow traffic"],"Hygiene protects health from exposures.")
H('417. d.4.C',4,"The hierarchy of controls says the best way to handle a hazard is to first try to:","eliminate it",["wear a mask","post a sign","ignore it"],"Elimination beats PPE.")
H('417. d.4.D',3,"A welder needs a face shield, while a concrete finisher needs waterproof boots. Matching gear to the hazard is the proper use of:","personal protective equipment",["site rumors","office supplies","paint samples"],"PPE depends on the task.")
H('417. d.4.D',4,"Hearing protection is required on a site when noise levels reach a point that could cause permanent:","hearing loss",["sleepiness","boredom","good mood"],"Noise exposure damages ears.")
H('417. d.4.E',3,"Keeping walkways clear of tools and debris reduces the chance that a worker will suffer a:","trip and fall",["sunburn","paper cut","bad review"],"Housekeeping prevents falls.")
H('417. d.4.E',4,"Workers on a roof edge must use a guardrail system or a personal fall arrest system once the drop reaches:","six feet",["six miles","six inches","sixty feet"],"Construction fall protection begins at six feet.")
H('417. d.4.F',3,"Using a power tool with a missing ground pin can send current through the user, which is an electrical:","shock hazard",["noise hazard","color hazard","scheduling hazard"],"Grounding prevents shock.")
H('417. d.4.F',4,"Overhead power lines near a crane boom create a risk of:","electrocution",["boredom","rain delay","fashion issues"],"Cranes must stay clear of lines.")
H('417. d.4.G',3,"A worker needs to know the fire and health risks of a solvent before opening it, so she reads the:","safety data sheet",["menu","timesheet","gossip column"],"SDSs describe chemical hazards.")
H('417. d.4.G',4,"Compressed gas cylinders should be stored upright and secured so they cannot fall and:","break their valves",["look neat","get lost","cost less"],"Falling cylinders can become projectiles.")
H('417. d.4.H',3,"A map posted at the trailer showing the assembly point, first aid kit, and fire extinguishers is a worksite safety:","resource",["menu","joke","puzzle"],"Resources prepare workers.")
H('417. d.4.H',4,"Knowing where the nearest eyewash station is matters because chemical splashes in the eye require treatment within:","seconds",["weeks","months","years"],"Quick flushing reduces damage.")
H('417. d.4.I',3,"A system in which managers commit resources and workers help find hazards is the core of a written safety and health:","program",["marketing plan","hiring rule","parking policy"],"Programs organize safety.")
H('417. d.4.I',4,"A written program should include regular worksite inspections so hazards can be found and:","corrected",["admired","copied","photographed only"],"Inspections find problems to fix.")
H('417. d.4.J',3,"A written emergency plan names who calls 911, where crews gather, and how to account for everyone after an:","evacuation",["election","vacation","audit"],"Plans give specific roles.")
H('417. d.4.J',4,"Practicing the evacuation plan twice a year helps workers stay calm and move quickly when there is a real:","emergency",["lunch","award","holiday"],"Drills build readiness.")
H('417. d.4.K',3,"A hazard communication program requires that containers be labeled and that workers learn how to read the:","labels and data sheets",["menu boards","traffic signs","contracts"],"HazCom tells workers what they handle.")
H('417. d.4.K',4,"A skull-and-crossbones pictogram on a chemical label signals:","acute toxicity",["a bargain","a bakery","a bonus"],"Pictograms quickly show hazard type.")
H('417. d.4.L',3,"Safety rules say a new worker must be trained on the hazards of a task and the controls for them before starting the:","job",["lunch","vacation","review"],"Training precedes exposure.")
H('417. d.4.L',4,"A refresher course on fall protection every year helps workers remember what they have learned and update their:","knowledge",["wages","tools","uniforms"],"Retraining maintains skills.")
H('417. d.5.A',3,"A project engineer lists the tasks for a site design and ranks them so the ones that block other work are done:","first",["last","never","at random"],"Priorities follow dependencies.")
H('417. d.5.A',4,"Ranking tasks by their impact on the schedule helps the engineer protect the project's:","deadline",["logo","lobby","parking"],"Priority protects the finish date.")
H('417. d.5.B',3,"Tasks A (3 days), B (5 days), and C (2 days) must be done one after another. The critical path length is:","10 days",["5 days","3 days","15 days"],"3 + 5 + 2 = 10.")
H('417. d.5.B',4,"If task D can run alongside B and takes 2 days, D is not critical because B already takes:","longer",["less time","the same pay","fewer people"],"The longer parallel task controls.")
H('417. d.5.C',3,"A budget based on billable hours multiplies the hours estimated for each task by the engineer's:","hourly rate",["age","birth date","parking space"],"Fee = hours x rate.")
H('417. d.5.C',4,"A task estimated at 12 hours at 85 dollars per hour costs:","1,020 dollars",["97 dollars","102 dollars","10,200 dollars"],"12 x 85 = 1,020.")
H('417. d.5.D',3,"Engineers record the hours they spend on each task on a timesheet so the firm can bill the client and see how the work compares with the:","budget",["weather","menu","song list"],"Timekeeping tracks cost.")
H('417. d.5.D',4,"Time tracked at 30 hours against a 24 hour estimate shows the task has gone:","over budget",["under budget","exactly on budget","unbilled"],"Overruns signal a problem.")
H('417. d.5.E',3,"A Gantt chart for a design project lists tasks down the side and shows bars across a:","time scale",["menu","map","recipe"],"Gantt bars show time.")
H('417. d.5.E',4,"Dependency arrows between bars on a Gantt chart show which tasks must be complete before another can:","begin",["be named","be priced","be photographed"],"Links show order.")
H('417. d.5.F',3,"Creating folders for each discipline and phase at the start of a job is developing a systematic:","folder structure",["trophy case","calendar","dress code"],"Structure keeps files findable.")
H('417. d.5.F',4,"A shared folder structure saves time because team members always know where to put and find the:","latest files",["lunch orders","vacation requests","office plants"],"Consistency speeds retrieval.")
H('417. d.5.G',3,"A rule that every drawing file begins with the project number, then the sheet type, then the revision is a file:","naming convention",["law of motion","traffic code","price list"],"Conventions standardize names.")
H('417. d.5.G',4,"Applying naming rules to emails, drawings, and reports alike lets anyone on the team search and sort the project's:","documents",["lunches","vacations","timecards only"],"Uniform names enable searching.")
H('417. d.5.H',3,"Reviewing each drawing set against a checklist before release is a best management practice called quality:","control",["delay","trouble","decor"],"QC catches errors.")
H('417. d.5.H',4,"A best management practice such as peer review helps a firm deliver work that is accurate and:","consistent",["late","vague","hidden"],"BMPs standardize quality.")
H('417. d.5.I',3,"Checking that a site plan meets city zoning, state environmental rules, and federal accessibility law is evaluating adherence to:","regulations",["opinions","trends","slogans"],"Compliance checks cover all levels.")
H('417. d.5.I',4,"A project that skips a required state permit may be ordered to stop work and pay:","fines",["bonuses","awards","interest"],"Noncompliance has penalties.")
H('417. d.5.J',3,"Checking that a design follows firm standards for QA reviews, document control, and safety is evaluating adherence to best management:","practices",["rumors","moods","fashions"],"BMPs are checked for each project.")
H('417. d.5.J',4,"An audit that finds missed review steps allows the firm to improve its:","procedures",["logo","building","uniform"],"Audits improve processes.")
H('417. d.5.K',3,"Reviewing a design for water-saving fixtures, recycled materials, and energy efficiency is evaluating the implementation of:","sustainable practices",["noise practices","photo practices","tax practices"],"Sustainability is measured in features.")
H('417. d.5.K',4,"A sustainable practice might cost more at first but save money over the building's:","life cycle",["birthday","address","paint job"],"Life-cycle cost considers long-term savings.")
H('417. d.6.A',3,"The project manual for a construction job holds the contract conditions, specifications, and the:","bid documents",["lunch menu","trophies","playlists"],"The manual compiles written documents.")
H('417. d.6.A',4,"Divisions in a project manual group the specifications by trade, such as concrete, metals, and:","finishes",["gossip","parties","vacations"],"Spec divisions follow a standard.")
H('417. d.6.B',3,"The bid process includes advertising the job, a pre-bid meeting, receiving bids, and awarding the contract to the lowest:","responsible bidder",["relative","guess","cousin"],"Awards go to qualified low bidders.")
H('417. d.6.B',4,"Value engineering during bidding asks whether the project's function can be provided at a lower:","cost",["height","elevation","age"],"VE finds savings without losing function.")
H('417. d.6.C',3,"A quantity take-off for a sidewalk measures its length, width, and thickness to find the volume of:","concrete needed",["music played","paint on signs","cars parked"],"Take-offs convert plans into quantities.")
H('417. d.6.C',4,"A sidewalk is 100 ft long, 5 ft wide, and 0.33 ft thick. Its volume is about:","165 cubic feet",["16.5 cubic feet","500 cubic feet","1,650 cubic feet"],"100 x 5 x 0.33 = 165.")
H('417. d.6.D',3,"The specifications call for 4,000 psi concrete, so the contractor must order a mix that meets that:","strength",["color","smell","price"],"Specs define required properties.")
H('417. d.6.D',4,"Materials that are not named or approved in the specifications can be rejected by the engineer, so the contractor checks the specs before:","ordering",["inspecting","lunch","closing"],"Verify before purchase.")
H('417. d.7.A',3,"A shop drawing prepared by a fabricator is compared with the construction documents to find and fix any:","discrepancies",["colors","jokes","rumors"],"Shop drawings must conform.")
H('417. d.7.A',4,"If a shop drawing shows a steel beam smaller than the design drawings, the engineer should:","reject or mark it for correction",["approve it","skip the review","hide it"],"Review prevents under-sized parts.")
H('417. d.7.B',3,"A contractor proposes a different brand of pipe and the engineer checks that it meets the project's material:","specifications",["rumors","decorations","taglines"],"Substitutions must be justified.")
H('417. d.7.B',4,"To justify a substitute material, the contractor provides data showing it equals or exceeds the specified:","performance",["price only","color only","brand only"],"Equivalency is shown by data.")
H('417. d.7.C',3,"A submittal log lists every item the contractor must submit for review and the dates each is:","received and returned",["promised and forgotten","painted and framed","named and filed away"],"Logs track status.")
H('417. d.7.C',4,"Organizing material specifications by spec section makes it easier to build a complete:","submittal log",["lunch order","wedding list","guest list"],"Sections map to submittals.")
H('417. d.7.D',3,"While reviewing a drawing, an engineer notes a duct crossing a beam and writes a design:","question",["song","menu","poem"],"Questions resolve conflicts early.")
H('417. d.7.D',4,"A request for information (RFI) is sent when the contractor needs the designer to clarify unclear or conflicting:","drawings or specs",["lunch plans","weather data","pet names"],"RFIs clear up documents.")
H('417. d.7.E',3,"Before beginning many projects, owners must get approval from authorities, a process called:","permitting",["festivals","audits","tailoring"],"Permits authorize work.")
H('417. d.7.E',4,"The approval process for a building generally includes submitting an application, review by the agency, and the issuance of a:","permit",["rumor","ticket to a game","coupon"],"Permits are issued after review.")
H('417. d.7.F',3,"In permitting, the reviewing city staff member and the applicant's engineer are both permitting:","stakeholders",["rivals","tourists","audiences"],"Stakeholders include applicants and reviewers.")
H('417. d.7.F',4,"The fire marshal reviews the plans for fire access, while the health department reviews plans for:","sanitary facilities",["parking colors","party plans","lobby decor"],"Each agency has a role.")
H('417. d.7.G',3,"A project that discharges stormwater to a creek needs a permit request to the state agency, which in Texas is the:","TCEQ",["NFL","NBA","FIFA"],"TCEQ issues stormwater permits.")
H('417. d.7.G',4,"A building permit request goes to the local city or county permitting:","office",["orchestra","bakery","cinema"],"Local offices handle building permits.")
H('417. d.7.H',3,"A change order is a written document that modifies the contract's scope, price, or:","schedule",["font","color","name"],"Change orders alter the contract.")
H('417. d.7.H',4,"A change order should state the reason for the change, the cost, and any time extension, and it must be signed by the owner and:","contractor",["tourist","neighbor","competitor"],"Both parties approve.")
H('417. d.7.I',3,"A log that lists each change request, its date, its cost, and its status is a method of tracking project:","changes",["rumors","lunches","vacations"],"Change logs keep order.")
H('417. d.7.I',4,"Tracking changes in one place helps the owner see how many changes have been approved and how much the total has gone:","up",["sideways","sour","blue"],"Cumulative impact is visible.")
H('417. d.7.J',3,"A certificate of substantial completion states the project is ready for its intended:","use",["advertising","celebration","retirement"],"The certificate marks readiness.")
H('417. d.7.J',4,"Final completion documents include the punch list sign-off, warranties, and record drawings turned over to the:","owner",["competitor","reporter","vendor"],"The owner receives closeout documents.")
H('417. d.8.A',3,"The Environmental Protection Agency is a federal regulatory agency that sets rules for air, water, and:","waste",["music","bakeries","sports"],"The EPA regulates the environment.")
H('417. d.8.A',4,"The U.S. Army Corps of Engineers requires a federal permit before a project may place fill in:","wetlands and waters of the U.S.",["parking lots","rooftops","private offices"],"Section 404 regulates fill.")
H('417. d.8.B',3,"The Texas Department of Transportation regulates the design and use of state:","highways",["restaurants","parks only","theaters"],"TxDOT oversees state roads.")
H('417. d.8.B',4,"A driveway that connects to a state highway typically needs an access permit from:","TxDOT",["a bakery","a bank","a school"],"State roads are permitted by the state.")
H('417. d.8.C',3,"A city planning department reviews site plans to make sure they follow local zoning and:","ordinances",["fashion","rumors","tastes"],"Cities enforce local rules.")
H('417. d.8.C',4,"County agencies often regulate drainage and septic systems in areas that lie:","outside city limits",["inside city hall","inside stadiums","inside banks"],"Counties govern unincorporated areas.")
H('417. d.8.D',3,"A local ordinance that requires a minimum number of parking spaces per square foot of building is a:","zoning requirement",["tax cut","free pass","rumor"],"Zoning sets parking ratios.")
H('417. d.8.D',4,"To address a building code requirement, a designer reads the adopted code and then shows compliance on the:","plans",["menus","tickets","brochures"],"Plans demonstrate compliance.")
H('417. d.9.A',3,"Transferring the risk of a flood loss to an insurance company is a risk management method called:","risk transfer",["risk worship","risk music","risk decor"],"Insurance transfers risk.")
H('417. d.9.A',4,"Moving a building site out of a flood zone to avoid damage is the risk method of:","avoidance",["acceptance","transfer","delay"],"Avoidance removes the exposure.")
H('417. d.9.B',3,"A risk analysis for a new pipeline lists possible problems and rates each for likelihood and:","impact",["color","size of font","age of staff"],"Risk ranks probability and impact.")
H('417. d.9.B',4,"A risk that is unlikely but would be catastrophic, such as a dam failure, still needs a:","mitigation plan",["celebration","blank sheet","party"],"High consequence demands planning.")
H('417. d.9.C',3,"A job hazard analysis breaks a task into steps, identifies hazards in each step, and lists ways to:","control them",["admire them","ignore them","sell them"],"JHAs reduce hazards.")
H('417. d.9.C',4,"A JHA for trench excavation would list cave-in as a hazard and sloping or shoring as a:","control",["problem","surprise","rumor"],"Controls address hazards.")
H('417. d.9.D',3,"Unexpected costs, such as finding rock during excavation, are covered in a budget by adding a:","contingency",["trophy","bonus","vacation"],"Contingency covers unknowns.")
H('417. d.9.D',4,"A contingency is usually set as a percentage of the project cost and becomes larger as uncertainty:","increases",["decreases","vanishes","stops"],"More uncertainty needs more cushion.")
H('417. d.9.E',3,"A contingency estimate lists events that could add money to a project, such as weather delays, and assigns each an expected:","cost",["color","name","hobby"],"Estimates quantify risk.")
H('417. d.9.E',4,"A 10 percent chance of a 50,000 dollar cost increase adds an expected value of:","5,000 dollars",["500 dollars","50,000 dollars","10 dollars"],"0.10 x 50,000 = 5,000.")
H('417. d.9.F',3,"A risk management plan presented to a client describes the major risks, how likely each is, and who will manage:","each one",["the lobby","the parking","the lunch"],"Plans assign ownership.")
H('417. d.9.F',4,"Presenting a risk management plan in plain language helps the client decide how much risk to:","accept",["ignore","create","hide"],"Clear plans support decisions.")
H('417. d.10.A',3,"Value engineering is a review aimed at providing the needed function at the lowest:","life-cycle cost",["quality","height","speed only"],"VE preserves function and cuts cost.")
H('417. d.10.A',4,"Value engineering is not simply cutting quality because it keeps the project's required:","function and performance",["decoration","slogan","marketing"],"VE protects the essentials.")
H('417. d.10.B',3,"Large cost items, such as site earthwork and structural frames, are areas where a project is most susceptible to:","cost savings or overruns",["music","gossip","dust only"],"Big items drive cost.")
H('417. d.10.B',4,"Reviewing the highest-cost items first in a value engineering study is efficient because small changes there can save the most:","money",["paint","time on lunch","space"],"Focus on big costs.")
H('417. d.10.C',3,"Comparing the cost estimate with the design to find items that cost more than they add in value is a:","savings search",["party","poem","rumor"],"Analysis finds potential savings.")
H('417. d.10.C',4,"An option that replaces custom steel with a standard shape may save money while still meeting the:","design requirements",["marketing needs","guest list","paint plan"],"Standardization often reduces cost.")
H('417. d.10.D',3,"An opinion of probable cost is the engineer's estimate of what a project is likely to cost to:","build",["admire","visit","name"],"OPCs forecast construction cost.")
H('417. d.10.D',4,"An OPC is called an opinion because the actual cost depends on the market and the contractor's:","bid",["height","logo","hometown"],"Prices vary with the market.")
H('417. d.10.E',3,"An OPC includes the cost of materials and labor as well as contractor overhead, profit, and construction:","mobilization",["birthdays","vacations","parties"],"OPCs list all cost types.")
H('417. d.10.E',4,"Materials of 120,000 dollars, labor of 80,000 dollars, and mobilization of 20,000 dollars total:","220,000 dollars",["200,000 dollars","100,000 dollars","320,000 dollars"],"120 + 80 + 20 = 220 thousand.")
H('417. d.10.F',3,"An economic study of a flood wall adds up the money saved from avoided damage and compares that total with the wall's:","cost",["color","height only","name"],"Benefits are compared with costs.")
H('417. d.10.F',4,"Benefits of 600,000 dollars and costs of 400,000 dollars give a benefit-cost ratio of:","1.5",["0.67","2.0","200,000"],"600/400 = 1.5.")
H('417. d.11.A',3,"On an engineering project team, the person who leads the work, assigns tasks, and communicates with the client is the:","project manager",["intern from another firm","vendor","tourist"],"The PM leads the team.")
H('417. d.11.A',4,"A drafter or CAD technician on a team primarily prepares the:","drawings",["budget policy","legal contracts","bids"],"Drafters create plan sheets.")
H('417. d.11.B',3,"Agile and waterfall are two project management:","methodologies",["foods","sports","songs"],"Methodologies organize the work.")
H('417. d.11.B',4,"Waterfall completes each phase in order before the next, while Agile works in short cycles with frequent:","feedback",["silence","vacations","delays"],"Agile iterates with feedback.")
H('417. d.11.C',3,"A schedule of roles shows who is responsible for each task and when each person is:","needed",["bored","late","paid"],"Role schedules assign work.")
H('417. d.11.C',4,"Listing a backup for each key role helps the project continue when a team member is:","absent",["promoted to owner","too early","overpaid"],"Backups protect the schedule.")
H('417. d.11.D',3,"A kick-off meeting introduces the project's goals, scope, roles, and the plan for how the team will:","communicate",["decorate","vacation","celebrate"],"Kick-off sets expectations.")
H('417. d.11.D',4,"An effective kick-off meeting ends with clear action items and:","assigned owners and dates",["silence","blank notes","a long break"],"Actions need ownership.")
H('417. d.11.E',3,"A team in which members respect one another and share the workload will usually complete the project more:","successfully",["slowly","poorly","randomly"],"Healthy dynamics help results.")
H('417. d.11.E',4,"A team member who regularly misses deadlines can harm the project by pushing back the work of those who:","depend on that task",["arrive first","like the office","have more tools"],"Dependencies make delays contagious.")
H('417. d.11.F',3,"A meeting agenda lists the topics, the time for each, and the person who will:","lead each item",["bring snacks","book flights","choose music"],"Agendas focus meetings.")
H('417. d.11.F',4,"Sending the agenda before the meeting lets attendees come prepared, which makes the meeting more:","efficient",["costly","confusing","lengthy"],"Preparation improves meetings.")
H('417. d.11.G',3,"Meeting minutes record the decisions made, the action items, and who is:","responsible",["late","funny","absent for lunch"],"Minutes document accountability.")
H('417. d.11.G',4,"Minutes should be distributed soon after the meeting so everyone has the same understanding of what was:","agreed",["eaten","worn","drawn"],"Prompt minutes avoid confusion.")
H('417. d.11.H',3,"Qualities of an effective leader include honesty, clear communication, and the ability to:","listen",["avoid people","hide goals","dodge work"],"Good leaders listen.")
H('417. d.11.H',4,"A leader who admits a mistake and corrects it builds trust, which makes team members more willing to share:","problems early",["gossip","complaints about lunch","credit"],"Trust surfaces issues.")
H('417. d.11.I',3,"A leader who gives clear directions and makes decisions alone is using an authoritative style, while one who asks the team for ideas uses a:","participative style",["silent style","random style","hidden style"],"Styles differ in team involvement.")
H('417. d.11.I',4,"Choosing a leadership style should depend on the situation, such as an emergency, where a quick decision calls for:","a directive approach",["a long poll","no direction","a public vote"],"Emergencies need clear direction.")
H('417. d.11.J',3,"A student who is good at organizing and encouraging others might describe her leadership strength as:","coordination and motivation",["avoiding people","hiding tasks","delaying deadlines"],"Self-awareness identifies strengths.")
H('417. d.11.J',4,"Knowing your own weaknesses as a leader, such as difficulty delegating, lets you take steps to:","improve",["conceal them","ignore them","blame others"],"Awareness enables growth.")
H('417. d.11.K',3,"A student leader who sets clear expectations and recognizes teammates' work will probably see the team's project outcome:","improve",["decline","freeze","vanish"],"Leadership affects results.")
H('417. d.11.K',4,"Reflecting on how your leadership affected the outcome helps you decide what to do differently on the next:","project",["hobby","lunch","vacation"],"Reflection builds skills.")

